---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from "@/components/ui/card";
import { createI18n } from "@maplespike/i18n";

const lang = (Astro.props.lang as "en" | "fr") || "en";
const i18n = createI18n(lang);
---

<BaseLayout title={i18n.t('terms.title')} description="MapleSpike terms of service — the agreement between you and MapleSpike." lang={lang}>
  <section class="border-b py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
        {i18n.t('terms.title')}
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">{i18n.t('terms.last_updated', { date: 'July 1, 2026' })}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container mx-auto px-4 py-12 md:py-16 max-w-3xl">
    <div class="space-y-8">
      <Card>
        <CardHeader>
          <CardTitle class="text-lg">1. Acceptance of Terms</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-3">
          <p>By accessing or using MapleSpike's API, web portal, MCP tools, or SDKs ("the Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.</p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <Card>
        <CardHeader>
          <CardTitle class="text-lg">2. Description of Service</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-3">
          <p>MapleSpike provides a unified API for Canadian government data, including but not limited to: parliamentary committees, lobbying registries, procurement records, regulatory filings, court decisions, and statistical data. The Service includes REST API access, MCP server integration for AI agents, TypeScript and Python SDKs, and a web-based data explorer.</p>
          <p>All data served by MapleSpike is sourced from official Canadian government publications and is licensed under the Open Government Licence – Canada or equivalent provincial open data licenses.</p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <Card>
        <CardHeader>
          <CardTitle class="text-lg">3. Acceptable Use</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-3">
          <p>You agree NOT to:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li>Use the Service to violate any Canadian law or regulation</li>
            <li>Attempt to reverse-engineer, decompile, or circumvent rate limits or authentication</li>
            <li>Resell or redistribute raw API data without attribution as required by OGL-Canada</li>
            <li>Use the Service for automated scraping that exceeds your plan's rate limits</li>
            <li>Submit queries designed to extract personal information about identifiable individuals</li>
            <li>Use AI-generated content from the Service without verification for factual accuracy</li>
          </ul>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <Card>
        <CardHeader>
          <CardTitle class="text-lg">4. Plans, Billing & Refunds</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-3">
          <p>Free tier includes 1,000 API calls per month with no credit card required. Paid plans — Pro ($50 CAD/month) and Business ($200 CAD/month) — unlock higher rate limits and additional features as described on our <a href="/pricing" class="text-primary hover:underline">pricing page</a>.</p>
          <p><strong>Payment.</strong> Subscriptions are processed by <a href="https://stripe.com" class="text-primary hover:underline" rel="noopener">Stripe</a>. Prices are in Canadian dollars (CAD). Taxes (e.g. GST/HST) are added at checkout where applicable.</p>
          <p><strong>Billing cycle.</strong> Paid plans are billed in advance on a monthly cycle. Your subscription renews automatically until cancelled.</p>
          <p><strong>Cancellation.</strong> You may cancel at any time from your account dashboard. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period; you retain paid access until then. No partial-period refund is issued on cancellation, but you keep what you paid for through period end.</p>
          <p id="refunds"><strong>Refunds.</strong> If you are dissatisfied within <strong>14 days</strong> of your first payment on a new paid plan, contact <a href="mailto:billing@maplespike.ca" class="text-primary hover:underline">billing@maplespike.ca</a> for a full refund of that charge — no questions asked. Renewal charges beyond the first 14 days are non-refundable, except where required by law or where a service outage breaches our stated SLA.</p>
          <p><strong>Failed payments.</strong> If a renewal charge fails, we retry and may downgrade your tier to Free at the end of the grace period; no data is deleted.</p>
          <p>Our refund and cancellation terms are also summarized at checkout. By subscribing you acknowledge having read this section and our <a href="/privacy" class="text-primary hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <Card>
        <CardHeader>
          <CardTitle class="text-lg">5. Citation & Attribution</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-3">
          <p>Every API response includes a citation block with source name, source URL, SHA-256 content hash, and license type. You are responsible for including appropriate attribution when using MapleSpike data in publications, reports, or AI training datasets.</p>
          <p>The required attribution format is: <code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-muted rounded text-xs font-mono">[Source name], retrieved [date] via MapleSpike. OGL-Canada.</code></p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <Card>
        <CardHeader>
          <CardTitle class="text-lg">6. Data Accuracy Disclaimer</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-3">
          <p>While MapleSpike uses SHA-256 content hashing and trust-score validation to ensure data integrity, we do not guarantee the accuracy, completeness, or timeliness of government source data. Every response includes a <code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-muted rounded text-xs font-mono">quality</code> object with freshness and confidence metrics.</p>
          <p>For legal or regulatory decisions, always verify data directly with the original source using the provided citation URL and content hash.</p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <Card>
        <CardHeader>
          <CardTitle class="text-lg">7. Limitation of Liability</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-3">
          <p>MapleSpike is provided "as is" without warranty of any kind. We are not liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from the use of the Service, including but not limited to decisions made based on data served by the API.</p>
          <p>Our total liability for any claim shall not exceed the amount you paid for the Service in the 12 months preceding the claim.</p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <Card>
        <CardHeader>
          <CardTitle class="text-lg">8. Changes to Terms</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-3">
          <p>We may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes will be announced via the <a href="/changelog" class="text-primary hover:underline">changelog</a> and emailed to registered users at least 30 days before taking effect.</p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <Card>
        <CardHeader>
          <CardTitle class="text-lg">9. Contact</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-3">
          <p>Questions about these Terms? Email <a href="mailto:legal@maplespike.ca" class="text-primary hover:underline">legal@maplespike.ca</a> or use our <a href="/contact" class="text-primary hover:underline">contact form</a>.</p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
